From d72f3e654b664c0c60844539bcc3c29052c617ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DryhoppedIPA <DryhoppedIPA@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 04:53:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] radv,aco: native mesh and task shaders on GFX1013

Rebase the experimental GFX1013 mesh/task path. Keep the GFX1013 hardware
workarounds from the original patch, but require a GFX10.3 software level for
exposing mesh/task features so the path stays dormant until RADV_GFX103 is
explicitly enabled.

Rebased onto Mesa main after 5d95a8f141d removed the driver-side workaround for
has_taskmesh_indirect0_bug. That workaround was what this patch extended for
GFX1013's extra zero-dimensional ACE hang, so the four hunks refining it are
gone. Mesh shading is kept; task shading is now reported unsupported on GFX1013
rather than exposed on top of a workaround upstream no longer carries, which
matches where it already stood in practice.
